.TH HARNESS 1 "September 2026" "agent-harness 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
harness \- performance layer for coding agents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B harness
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Skills, instincts, memory, security and research-first that works the same
in Claude Code, Codex, Opencode, Cursor, Kiro CLI and Kiro.
.PP
Run \fBharness init\fR in your project, then \fBharness doctor\fR to verify.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init [--harness <name>] [--auto] [--migrate]
Set up harness in current project.
.TP
.B doctor [--fix] [--strict]
Check adapters, skills, security.
.TP
.B bench [--compare] [--quick]
Measure costs, save baseline.
.TP
.B optimize
Prune memory, repair, report savings.
.TP
.B skill list
List skills with cost.
.TP
.B memory <show|prune>
Show or prune MEMORY.md.
.TP
.B instinct list
List hooks.
.TP
.B adapter list
List supported harnesses.
.TP
.B upgrade
Self-update to latest.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR https://github.com/TheElephantCoder/agent-harness
